[
 {
  "start": 0.2,
  "end": 19.0,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 0.38,
  "end": 1.24,
  "text": "*One couple.*",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 2.7,
  "end": 5.16,
  "text": "That means a *date*.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 5.74,
  "end": 8.02,
  "text": "Not like just going around with the crowd.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 9.28,
  "end": 10.78,
  "text": "Just me and the girl.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 11.98,
  "end": 13.88,
  "text": "Well, that's all right.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 15.36,
  "end": 17.56,
  "text": "Only... *what girl?*",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 18.46,
  "end": 19.2,
  "text": "Who?",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 19.5,
  "end": 30.7,
  "text": "The Strange Dating Rules\\NAmerican Schools Taught in 1949",
  "style": "TITLE"
 },
 {
  "start": 20.4,
  "end": 30.7,
  "text": "\\N\\N\\N\\N\\N\\NAn AI-restored archival documentary demo",
  "style": "SUBTITLE"
 },
 {
  "start": 26.2,
  "end": 34.2,
  "text": "Dating: Do's and Don'ts (1949)\\NCoronet Instructional Films \u00b7 Glenview, Illinois \u00b7 Kodachrome print",
  "style": "ANNOT"
 },
 {
  "start": 39.7,
  "end": 56.699999999999996,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 39.74,
  "end": 42.02,
  "text": "*How do you choose a date?*",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 39.9,
  "end": 44.0,
  "text": "I. Choosing the girl",
  "style": "CHAPTER"
 },
 {
  "start": 43.04,
  "end": 44.46,
  "text": "Whose company would you enjoy?",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 45.76,
  "end": 48.06,
  "text": "Well, one thing you can consider is *looks*.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 50.58,
  "end": 53.12,
  "text": "Woody thought of Janice and how good-looking she was.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 53.86,
  "end": 56.6,
  "text": "He'd really have to *rate* to date somebody like her.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 57.1,
  "end": 72.1,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 57.14,
  "end": 58.18,
  "text": "What about Ann?",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 59.06,
  "end": 62.8,
  "text": "She knows how to have a good time, and how to make the fellow with her *relax*.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 63.04,
  "end": 63.82,
  "text": "Have fun, too.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 65.36,
  "end": 67.2,
  "text": "Yes, that's what a boy likes.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 67.7,
  "end": 69.38,
  "text": "He wants to know he's *appreciated*.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 70.2,
  "end": 71.76,
  "text": "Ann would be fun on a date.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 90.1,
  "end": 98.9,
  "text": "Educational collaborator: Reuben Hill\\NResearch Professor of Family Life, University of North Carolina",
  "style": "ANNOT"
 },
 {
  "start": 100.8,
  "end": 117.39999999999999,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 100.88,
  "end": 102.94,
  "text": "Ann? This is Woody.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 101.0,
  "end": 105.1,
  "text": "II. Asking for a date",
  "style": "CHAPTER"
 },
 {
  "start": 103.92,
  "end": 108.48,
  "text": "Well, I have a ticket for the Hi-Teen Carnival Saturday, and...",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 108.48,
  "end": 109.44,
  "text": "Well, would you like to go?",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 110.9,
  "end": 111.86,
  "text": "Why, yes, Woody.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 112.48,
  "end": 114.18,
  "text": "I'll have to talk to *my folks* about it.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 114.28,
  "end": 117.18,
  "text": "But I think I can go. That'll be fine.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 131.6,
  "end": 144.6,
  "text": "Median age at first marriage, 1950\\Nwomen 20.3 \u00b7 men 22.8   (U.S. Census Bureau, table MS-2)",
  "style": "ANNOT"
 },
 {
  "start": 149.1,
  "end": 152.34,
  "text": "Well, if you don't *overdo* on dating...",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 149.1,
  "end": 156.70000000000002,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 149.3,
  "end": 153.4,
  "text": "III. The rules at home",
  "style": "CHAPTER"
 },
 {
  "start": 153.26,
  "end": 156.64,
  "text": "Ed knows what I mean. *Weekends only*, and not too late.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 157.1,
  "end": 173.9,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 157.18,
  "end": 160.8,
  "text": "I think the important thing about a date is to *have a good time*.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 161.44,
  "end": 163.74,
  "text": "You don't need to spend a lot of money to do that.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 164.44,
  "end": 170.28,
  "text": "You just enjoy whatever you do, whether it's movies or parties or anything.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 171.02,
  "end": 173.76,
  "text": "And you leave your boyfriend *enough money*, so he'll ask you again.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 174.29999999999998,
  "end": 178.5,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 174.38,
  "end": 178.14,
  "text": "Any girl who can't be *ready on time* for a date isn't good enough for my boy.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 188.2,
  "end": 197.7,
  "text": "\"Teenager\" enters common use in the 1940s\\NSeventeen magazine founded 1944",
  "style": "ANNOT"
 },
 {
  "start": 209.2,
  "end": 223.20000000000002,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 209.28,
  "end": 211.72,
  "text": "But *how do you say good night?*",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 209.4,
  "end": 213.5,
  "text": "IV. Saying good night",
  "style": "CHAPTER"
 },
 {
  "start": 214.42,
  "end": 214.86,
  "text": "Perhaps...",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 216.94,
  "end": 218.1,
  "text": "Don't leave!",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 221.44,
  "end": 222.86,
  "text": "*1 a.m.*",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 223.6,
  "end": 233.4,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 223.86,
  "end": 225.18,
  "text": "Well, so long.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 227.84,
  "end": 229.72,
  "text": "Just like that.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 230.56,
  "end": 233.18,
  "text": "After all, a girl likes to know you've had a *good time*.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 233.79999999999998,
  "end": 257.6,
  "text": "ORIGINAL AUDIO \u00b7 1949",
  "style": "LABEL"
 },
 {
  "start": 233.86,
  "end": 236.04,
  "text": "Well, it's getting late.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 236.52,
  "end": 237.44,
  "text": "Yes, it is.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 238.0,
  "end": 240.18,
  "text": "I'd ask you in for a bite to eat if it weren't so late.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 241.7,
  "end": 245.12,
  "text": "Let's plan to get home in time for a *sandwich* or something next time.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 245.6,
  "end": 247.04,
  "text": "Say, that sounds good.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 247.5,
  "end": 248.56,
  "text": "I'll *call you* next week.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 248.88,
  "end": 249.32,
  "text": "Will you?",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 250.12,
  "end": 252.32,
  "text": "Well, thanks so much.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 252.72,
  "end": 253.82,
  "text": "I had a nice time.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 254.52,
  "end": 255.08,
  "text": "So did I.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 255.64,
  "end": 256.3,
  "text": "Good night, Woody.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 256.88,
  "end": 257.34,
  "text": "Night, Ann.",
  "style": "ORIG"
 },
 {
  "start": 268.8,
  "end": 277.8,
  "text": "Median age at first marriage, 2024\\Nwomen 28.6 \u00b7 men 30.5   (NCFMR / American Community Survey)",
  "style": "ANNOT"
 },
